#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""syncthing-addfolder -- create one encrypted Syncthing folder across the cluster.

  syncthing-addfolder [options] ID LABEL WRITER-PATH READER-PATH HUB-PATH
  syncthing-addfolder --undo [--yes] [--dry-run] [--log FILE] ID LABEL

  ID            the folder id: two groups of five over a-z without i and l, and 2-9
  LABEL         its label, the same on all three machines
  WRITER-PATH   its absolute path here, on the writer (bigfed); a directory
  READER-PATH   its absolute path on the other workstation (fedxps): absent or
                empty makes the fresh shape, a copy already there the join shape
  HUB-PATH      its absolute path on the hub (nousowl): a directory that does
                not exist yet (hub-3)

  --trash DIR       join: the reader's trashcan for the revert, absolute and
                    outside the folder; the join shape requires it
  --allow-outside   join: go on when the reader's local changes lie outside a
                    .git (the rehearsal's scratch trees)
  --hub-only        share through the hub alone, without the direct link (ws-16)
  --hub NAME        the hub's device name, when no folder here names it yet
  --peer NAME       the reader's device name, when the hub knows more than two
  --yes             answer every gate; otherwise each gate waits for Enter
  --dry-run         read all three machines, print the plan, write nothing
  --log FILE        append every line printed to FILE as well
  --undo            remove folder ID from the hub, then here, then the reader;
                    every file stays on disk
  -h                this text

Exit: 0 done (a dry run: nothing refused) . 1 stopped: a refusal, a gate that
      did not hold, a wait that ran out, his word, Ctrl-C . 2 could not
      determine: a machine that did not answer, a reading that failed, bad
      arguments

The successor of org/machines/syncthing-2026-09/bin/syncthing-addfolder (bash,
2026-09-15), rewritten for the transport campaign (org/machines/transport-2026-10,
rules.md -> mig-4, mig-3, hub-3, ws-7, ws-16; pilot.md -> "Seeding the pilot
folder", whose hand-run sequence of 2026-10-10 this follows: pilot/seeding.md).
It runs on the writer, bigfed, and reaches the hub and the reader as the gauge
does. Every lesson of the 2026-09 script still binds:

  - the hub's folder is receiveencrypted with staggered versioning (maxAge one
    year) and minDiskFree 1 % set in the same POST, in a new directory: the
    hub's <defaults><folder> template has no versioning, so a folder added the
    obvious way silently keeps no history, and two folders on one hub path drop
    every connection to the hub (hub-3);
  - folders are made by POST /rest/config/folders, never `syncthing cli config
    folders add`, which may land maxConflicts 0 (conflicts discarded with no
    copy, ws-7); maxConflicts 10, fsWatcherDelayS 2 and rescanIntervalS 3600
    are set in every POST and read back after it;
  - the hub device is bounced (paused and resumed) on each workstation after
    its folder exists, since an encrypted folder added to a live connection
    never pulls; the bounce is verified by the disconnect and the reconnect it
    causes, and a device paused by this tool is resumed however it exits;
  - bigfed's folder is written first, so that a password entered on the day the
    cluster is rebuilt is durable in bigfed's config.xml before anything else
    can fail; autoAcceptFolders false on every device of all three machines is
    a preflight check, so nothing can accept bigfed's offer in the window;
  - the cluster password is asked for once in the life of the cluster.

THE TWO SHAPES. The reader's path decides. Absent or empty: the fresh shape --
bigfed's folder (sendreceive), the hub's, then once the hub holds bigfed's set
the reader's (sendreceive), each device list self + hub (with the password) +
the other workstation over the direct link unless --hub-only. A copy already
there (a repository seeded by git, or the Desktop at the cutover): the join
shape, mig-3's gates 5 to 9 as the pilot ran them -- the reader added
receiveonly with versioning trashcan (cleanoutDays 0, fsPath --trash), bounced;
gate 7 holds once the reader's view of the hub carries the hub's own sequence
(its index has arrived; measured 2026-10-26 on 2.1.6: 0 before) and the global
counts and bytes agree with bigfed's; db/localchanged read and every path
printed, the run stopping for his word when any lies outside a .git; the
revert; gate 9 (no receive-only change left, the sha256 manifests of the two
trees equal under LC_ALL=C with .stfolder/ left out, git fsck clean under
GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0 for every .git in the reader's tree, the trashcan holding
what was listed); the switch to sendreceive with the hub's and bigfed's folder
sequences read before and after a watch (nothing sent); the reader's versioning
back to none; then the direct link shared, as the pilot did after its switch.
Both shapes end with every view at 100 with nothing needed and every view's
sequence equal to the device's own.

PREFLIGHT, before any write, on all three machines: Syncthing answers; global
announce, relays, NAT and crash reporting off; autoAcceptFolders false on every
device; the devices connected and not paused; the id's shape and the label;
no other folder with this label or a path that contains or lies inside this
one; no .stfolder marker under either workstation's path or above it; the hub's
directory absent, and on the dedicated volume when under ~/sync (findmnt);
this machine's gsync.role reads writer, and the reader's reads another role, or
its readerRepo names READER-PATH (an absent role refuses); a repository
at a folder's root ignores .stfolder/ (mig-4, 2026-10-10); one cluster password
on each workstation, the same on both (compared by an HMAC under a nonce drawn
for the run, in memory, never printed); the join's trashcan absolute, outside
the folder and outside every Syncthing folder, absent or empty; an absent hub or
reader path under a directory. A reading git or the filesystem cannot give is a
WARN, and the run stops with exit 2.

RE-RUNNABLE. A machine already holding the folder as specified is verified, not
re-created; one holding it differently stops the run. The states a run can
leave are bigfed alone, bigfed and the hub, or all three, and any other stops.
Every stop prints the undo (`--undo`: DELETE on the hub first, then bigfed,
then the reader; every file stays on disk -- measured 2026-10-26 on 2.1.6, a
workstation's marker goes and the hub's is renamed .stfolder.removed-<time>
beside its blobs).

GATES. Each waits for Enter on the terminal (/dev/tty), or is answered by
--yes: before the first write; in the join, before the reader's receive-only
POST, before the revert and before the switch. A gate's readings are printed
before it.

SECRETS. The API key of each machine is read from its own config.xml into a
header and never printed. The cluster password is read structurally from an
existing encrypted folder's device entry on the machine where the folder's body
is composed -- the remote mode composes it there -- so it never crosses the
wire, argv, stdout or a file. On the day the cluster is rebuilt, when this
machine holds no encrypted folder, it is asked for once on /dev/tty (echo off,
twice, refused when it holds whitespace or this command's own arguments, as the
2026-09 script learnt), and reaches a reader that holds none either inside the
program text ssh carries on stdin, never on disk or in argv.

REMOTE MODE. The hub and the reader are reached as `sync-check` reaches them:
this file is sent over `ssh -o BatchMode=yes HOST python3 -I - --remote OP
JSON` and answers with one JSON line; HOST is the device's name in the config,
and HOST-vpn the second door when the first does not connect (2 s), a door
that failed not being tried again in the run. A write is never retried through
the second door: ssh's exit 255 cannot say whether it ran, so the run stops and
a re-run verifies what is there. SYNC_CHECK_CONFIG names another config.xml,
the same variable the gauge reads, so one fixture setting serves both tools.

Clock times come from the clock: every line is stamped, --log appends the same
lines. Waits are scaled to the folder: 120 s plus a second per 2 MB and 0.02 s
per file of bigfed's copy, each progress line printed when its reading changes.

The suite's knobs (tests/sync/case_addfolder.py): SYNCTHING_ADDFOLDER_POLL
(seconds between readings, 2), SYNCTHING_ADDFOLDER_HOLD (seconds a bounce holds
the device paused, 5), SYNCTHING_ADDFOLDER_WATCH (seconds the switch is
watched, 60), SYNCTHING_ADDFOLDER_WAIT_SCALE (a factor on every wait, 1).
"""

import getpass
import hashlib
import hmac
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import shlex
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request
import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
MAX_CONFLICTS = 10
WATCH_DELAY_S = 2
RESCAN_S = 3600
NO_VERSIONING = {"type": "", "params": {}, "cleanupIntervalS": 3600, "fsPath": "", "fsType": "basic"}
HUB_VERSIONING = {"type": "staggered", "params": {"maxAge": "31536000"},
                  "cleanupIntervalS": 3600, "fsPath": "", "fsType": "basic"}
HUB_MIN_DISK_FREE = {"value": 1, "unit": "%"}
PHONE_HOME = ("globalAnnounceEnabled", "relaysEnabled", "natEnabled", "crashReportingEnabled")
SECRET_KEYS = {"encryptionPassword", "apikey", "apiKey", "password", "user"}
# The cluster's alphabet for a new id (pilot/seeding.md, 2026-10-10): a-z
# without i and l, and 2-9; two groups of five, 50 bits.
ID_RE = re.compile(r"[a-hjkm-z2-9]{5}-[a-hjkm-z2-9]{5}")
HOSTNAME_RE = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,252}")
REST_TIMEOUT = 30
STATUS_KEYS = ("state", "needTotalItems", "needBytes", "pullErrors", "errors", "error",
               "globalFiles", "globalDirectories", "globalSymlinks", "globalBytes",
               "localFiles", "localDirectories", "localSymlinks", "localBytes",
               "receiveOnlyChangedFiles", "receiveOnlyChangedDirectories",
               "receiveOnlyChangedSymlinks", "receiveOnlyChangedDeletes",
               "receiveOnlyTotalItems", "sequence")
VIEW_KEYS = ("completion", "needItems", "needDeletes", "needBytes", "remoteState", "sequence", "globalItems")


def env_seconds(name, default):
    """A positive number from the environment, else the default."""
    try:
        v = float(os.environ.get(name, default))
    except ValueError:
        return default
    return v if v > 0 else default


POLL = env_seconds("SYNCTHING_ADDFOLDER_POLL", 2.0)
HOLD = env_seconds("SYNCTHING_ADDFOLDER_HOLD", 5.0)
WATCH = env_seconds("SYNCTHING_ADDFOLDER_WATCH", 60.0)
WAIT_SCALE = env_seconds("SYNCTHING_ADDFOLDER_WAIT_SCALE", 1.0)
WAIT_FLOOR = 120.0
WAIT_RATE = 2e6          # bytes a second
WAIT_PER_FILE = 0.02     # seconds a file


# =============================================================================
# The machine side: what runs on each machine, here in-process or there over ssh
# =============================================================================
class OpFail(Exception):
    """A reading or a write on this machine that could not be done."""


def config_path():
    env = os.environ.get("SYNC_CHECK_CONFIG")
    if env:
        return env if os.path.exists(env) else None
    # Syncthing's own order (`syncthing paths`): a legacy configuration
    # directory holding a config.xml wins over the state directory.
    cands = []
    if os.environ.get("XDG_CONFIG_HOME"):
        cands.append(os.path.join(os.environ["XDG_CONFIG_HOME"], "syncthing", "config.xml"))
    cands.append(os.path.join(HOME, ".config", "syncthing", "config.xml"))
    state = os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME")
    if state and os.path.isabs(state):
        cands.append(os.path.join(state, "syncthing", "config.xml"))
    cands.append(os.path.join(HOME, ".local", "state", "syncthing", "config.xml"))
    for p in cands:
        if os.path.exists(p):
            return p
    return None


def q(s):
    return urllib.parse.quote(s, safe="")


class Local:
    """This machine's Syncthing: the address and key from config.xml, which is
    parsed for the fields needed and read afresh for every operation."""

    def __init__(self):
        p = config_path()
        if not p:
            raise OpFail("no Syncthing configuration on %s (SYNC_CHECK_CONFIG, or config.xml "
                         "under ~/.config/syncthing or ~/.local/state/syncthing)" % os.uname().nodename)
        self.path = p
        self.root = ET.parse(p).getroot()
        gui = self.root.find("gui")
        addr = (gui.findtext("address") or "127.0.0.1:8384").strip()
        if addr.startswith("0.0.0.0:"):
            addr = "127.0.0.1:" + addr.split(":", 1)[1]
        if addr.startswith("[::]:"):
            addr = "127.0.0.1:" + addr.split("]:", 1)[1]
        scheme = "https" if (gui.get("tls") or "false").lower() == "true" else "http"
        self.base = "%s://%s/rest/" % (scheme, addr)
        self.key = (gui.findtext("apikey") or "").strip()

    def call(self, path, method="GET", body=None, timeout=REST_TIMEOUT):
        """(status, json-or-text); status None when the daemon does not answer."""
        data = json.dumps(body).encode("utf-8") if body is not None else None
        req = urllib.request.Request(self.base + path, data=data, method=method,
                                     headers={"X-API-Key": self.key, "Content-Type": "application/json"})
        try:
            with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:
                text = r.read().decode("utf-8", "replace")
                status = r.status
        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
            return e.code, e.read().decode("utf-8", "replace")[:500]
        except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError, ValueError) as e:
            return None, "%s" % (getattr(e, "reason", None) or e)
        if not text.strip():
            return status, {}
        try:
            return status, json.loads(text)
        except ValueError:
            return status, text[:500]

    def must(self, path, method="GET", body=None, timeout=REST_TIMEOUT):
        st, r = self.call(path, method, body, timeout)
        if st != 200:
            raise OpFail("%s /rest/%s answered %s: %s" % (method, path.split("?")[0], st, str(r)[:200]))
        return r

    def folder(self, fid):
        """The folder's configuration with every password replaced by <set> or
        "", or None when this machine does not hold it."""
        st, f = self.call("config/folders/" + q(fid))
        if st == 404:
            return None
        if st != 200 or not isinstance(f, dict):
            raise OpFail("GET /rest/config/folders/%s answered %s" % (fid, st))
        return redact(f)

    def folder_raw(self, fid):
        """The same, with the password: held in this process only."""
        st, f = self.call("config/folders/" + q(fid))
        if st != 200 or not isinstance(f, dict):
            raise OpFail("GET /rest/config/folders/%s answered %s" % (fid, st))
        return f

    def passwords(self):
        """Every distinct encryption password in this machine's folders, from
        config.xml; held in memory, never returned."""
        seen = []
        for f in self.root.findall("folder"):
            for d in f.findall("device"):
                pw = d.findtext("encryptionPassword") or ""
                if pw.strip() and pw not in seen:
                    seen.append(pw)
        return seen


def redact(o):
    if isinstance(o, dict):
        return {k: (("<set>" if o[k] else "") if k in SECRET_KEYS else redact(v)) for k, v in o.items()}
    if isinstance(o, list):
        return [redact(x) for x in o]
    return o


def hub_hash(folder):
    """A digest of the device entries that carry a password, to show in-process
    that a PATCH of the device list left them as they were."""
    hub = sorted((d for d in folder.get("devices", []) if d.get("encryptionPassword")),
                 key=lambda d: d.get("deviceID", ""))
    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(hub, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()


def marker_above(start):
    """The nearest directory at or above `start` holding a .stfolder marker."""
    p = os.path.abspath(start)
    while True:
        if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(p, ".stfolder")):
            return p
        parent = os.path.dirname(p)
        if parent == p:
            return None
        p = parent


def path_facts(p, walk):
    """What the folder's path holds: existence, emptiness, the markers under it
    and above it, and (walk) its regular files' count and bytes."""
    f = {"path": p, "exists": os.path.lexists(p), "isdir": os.path.isdir(p), "realpath": os.path.realpath(p),
         "islink": os.path.islink(p), "marker_above": marker_above(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(p)))}
    if not f["exists"]:
        a = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(p))
        while not os.path.lexists(a):
            a = os.path.dirname(a)
        f["ancestor"] = a
        f["ancestor_isdir"] = os.path.isdir(a)
    if not f["isdir"]:
        return f
    try:
        names = os.listdir(p)
    except OSError as e:
        f["error"] = str(e)
        return f
    f["entries"] = len(names)
    f["empty"] = not names
    f["marker_here"] = os.path.isdir(os.path.join(p, ".stfolder"))
    f["repo_root"] = os.path.lexists(os.path.join(p, ".git"))
    if walk:
        below, errors = [], []
        files = nbytes = 0
        for dp, dns, fns in os.walk(p, onerror=lambda e: errors.append(str(e))):
            if dp != p and ".stfolder" in dns:
                below.append(os.path.relpath(os.path.join(dp, ".stfolder"), p))
            for n in fns:
                try:
                    st = os.lstat(os.path.join(dp, n))
                except OSError as e:
                    errors.append(str(e))
                    continue
                if not os.path.islink(os.path.join(dp, n)):
                    files += 1
                    nbytes += st.st_size
        f.update(markers_below=below[:20], markers_below_count=len(below),
                 files=files, bytes=nbytes, walk_errors=errors[:5])
    return f


def mount_facts(p):
    """Whether the hub path lies under ~/sync, and if so what is mounted where
    its parent is, read from findmnt's JSON."""
    sync = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(HOME, "sync"))
    rp = os.path.realpath(p)
    out = {"sync": sync, "applies": rp.startswith(sync + os.sep)}
    if not out["applies"]:
        return out
    out["exists"] = os.path.isdir(sync)
    if not out["exists"]:
        return out
    parent = os.path.dirname(rp)
    while not os.path.isdir(parent):
        parent = os.path.dirname(parent)
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["findmnt", "-J", "--target", parent], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20)
        fs = json.loads(r.stdout)["filesystems"][0]
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, ValueError, KeyError, IndexError) as e:
        raise OpFail("findmnt could not read the mount under %s: %s" % (parent, e))
    out.update(target=fs.get("target"), fstype=fs.get("fstype"), source=fs.get("source"))
    return out


def git_out(args, cwd="/", env_extra=None, timeout=60):
    env = dict(os.environ, GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS="0")
    if env_extra:
        env.update(env_extra)
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git"] + args, cwd=cwd, env=env, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return 127, "", "git not installed"
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return 124, "", "no answer within %d s" % timeout
    return r.returncode, r.stdout, r.stderr


def git_facts(p):
    """This machine's gsync.role and gsync.readerRepo keys through git's own
    config (the host include), each readerRepo resolved as 50-git-sync.sh
    resolves it, $HOME/Desktop/<value>; and whether a repository at the
    path's root ignores the marker. git exit 1 is "no such key"; above 1 the
    configuration could not be read."""
    rc, out, err = git_out(["config", "--get", "gsync.role"])
    f = {"role_rc": rc, "role": out.strip(), "role_err": err.strip()[:200]}
    rc, out, err = git_out(["config", "--get-all", "gsync.readerRepo"])
    repos = [v.strip() for v in out.splitlines() if v.strip()]
    want = os.path.realpath(p)
    f.update(reader_repo_rc=rc, reader_repo_err=err.strip()[:200], reader_repos=repos,
             reader_repo_match=any(os.path.realpath(HOME + "/Desktop/" + v) == want for v in repos))
    if os.path.lexists(os.path.join(p, ".git")):
        rc, out, err = git_out(["-C", p, "check-ignore", "-q", ".stfolder/syncthing-folder-check.txt"])
        f["marker_ignore_rc"] = rc
        f["marker_ignore_err"] = err.strip()[:200]
    return f


def trash_facts(t):
    f = {"path": t, "exists": os.path.lexists(t), "isdir": os.path.isdir(t),
         "marker_above": marker_above(t), "realpath": os.path.realpath(t)}
    if f["isdir"]:
        try:
            f["empty"] = not os.listdir(t)
        except OSError as e:
            f["error"] = str(e)
    return f


def op_probe(a):
    L = Local()
    s = L.must("system/status")
    out = {"myID": s.get("myID"), "startTime": s.get("startTime"), "config": L.path, "home": HOME,
           "node": os.uname().nodename}
    st, v = L.call("system/version")
    out["version"] = v.get("version") if isinstance(v, dict) else None
    o = L.must("config/options")
    out["options"] = {k: o.get(k) for k in PHONE_HOME}
    out["devices"] = [{k: d.get(k) for k in ("deviceID", "name", "autoAcceptFolders", "paused")}
                      for d in L.must("config/devices")]
    conns = (L.must("system/connections") or {}).get("connections") or {}
    out["connected"] = {did: bool(c.get("connected")) for did, c in conns.items()}
    out["folder"] = L.folder(a["fid"]) if a.get("fid") else None
    folders = []
    for f in L.root.findall("folder"):
        folders.append({"id": f.get("id"), "label": f.get("label") or "",
                        "path": os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser(f.get("path") or "")),
                        "type": f.get("type") or "sendreceive",
                        "enc": [d.get("id") for d in f.findall("device")
                                if (d.findtext("encryptionPassword") or "").strip()]})
    out["folders"] = folders
    pws = L.passwords()
    out["passwords"] = len(pws)
    if len(pws) == 1 and a.get("nonce"):
        out["pw_digest"] = hmac.new(a["nonce"].encode(), pws[0].encode("utf-8", "surrogateescape"),
                                    hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()
    pws = None
    if a.get("path"):
        out["path"] = path_facts(a["path"], a.get("walk", False))
        if a.get("git"):
            out["git"] = git_facts(a["path"])
        if a.get("mount"):
            out["mount"] = mount_facts(a["path"])
    if a.get("trash"):
        out["trash"] = trash_facts(a["trash"])
    return out


def op_post(a):
    """POST /rest/config/folders with the body the controller composed, the
    cluster password put into the hub's device entry here; the folder read
    back, redacted."""
    L = Local()
    body = a["body"]
    pw = None
    if a.get("enc_to"):
        if a.get("password") == "controller":
            pw = globals().get("_CONTROLLER_PASSWORD")
            if not isinstance(pw, str) or not pw:
                raise OpFail("no password came with the program text")
        else:
            pws = L.passwords()
            if len(pws) != 1:
                raise OpFail("this machine holds %d distinct cluster passwords, not one" % len(pws))
            pw = pws[0]
        hit = [d for d in body["devices"] if d.get("deviceID") == a["enc_to"]]
        if len(hit) != 1:
            raise OpFail("the body names the hub %d times" % len(hit))
        hit[0]["encryptionPassword"] = pw
    try:
        st, r = L.call("config/folders", "POST", body, timeout=120)
    finally:
        if pw:
            for d in body["devices"]:
                d.pop("encryptionPassword", None)
    text = "" if st == 200 else str(r)
    if pw and pw in text:
        text = text.replace(pw, "<password>")
    pw = None
    return {"code": st, "text": text[:300], "folder": L.folder(body["id"])}


def op_patch(a):
    """PATCH the folder's type, versioning or paused state; never its devices."""
    fields = a["fields"]
    if set(fields) - {"type", "versioning", "paused"}:
        raise OpFail("patch takes type, versioning and paused alone")
    L = Local()
    st, r = L.call("config/folders/" + q(a["fid"]), "PATCH", fields)
    return {"code": st, "text": "" if st == 200 else str(r)[:300], "folder": L.folder(a["fid"])}


def op_share(a):
    """Append one device (the direct link, no password) to the folder's device
    list; the entries carrying a password compared before and after, here."""
    L = Local()
    f = L.folder_raw(a["fid"])
    h0 = hub_hash(f)
    devs = f.get("devices") or []
    if any(d.get("deviceID") == a["device"] for d in devs):
        return {"code": 200, "already": True, "hub_entry_unchanged": True, "folder": L.folder(a["fid"])}
    st, r = L.call("config/folders/" + q(a["fid"]), "PATCH", {"devices": devs + [{"deviceID": a["device"]}]})
    f = devs = None
    f2 = L.folder_raw(a["fid"])
    same = hub_hash(f2) == h0
    f2 = None
    return {"code": st, "text": "" if st == 200 else str(r)[:300], "already": False,
            "hub_entry_unchanged": same, "folder": L.folder(a["fid"])}


def connection(L, did):
    conns = (L.must("system/connections") or {}).get("connections") or {}
    c = conns.get(did) or {}
    return bool(c.get("connected")), c.get("startedAt") or ""


def real_time(t):
    return bool(t) and not t.startswith("0001-")


BOUNCE = {}     # this process's bounce in flight: what an interruption reports


def op_bounce(a):
    """Pause the device, see the connection drop, hold, resume, see it come
    back. The resume runs however this exits. startedAt flips between the zero
    time and the real one from read to read (secondary connections, measured
    2026-10-26), so the first real value after the reconnect is the one kept."""
    L = Local()
    did, hold = a["device"], float(a.get("hold", 5))
    _, before = connection(L, did)
    t0 = time.time()
    dropped = None
    resumed = None
    BOUNCE.clear()
    BOUNCE["device"] = did
    try:
        BOUNCE["pause_sent"] = True
        st, r = L.call("config/devices/" + q(did), "PATCH", {"paused": True})
        if st != 200:
            raise OpFail("PATCH paused true answered %s: %s" % (st, str(r)[:200]))
        while time.time() - t0 < max(hold, 10.0):
            up, _ = connection(L, did)
            if not up:
                dropped = round(time.time() - t0, 2)
                break
            time.sleep(0.2)
        left = hold - (time.time() - t0)
        if left > 0:
            time.sleep(left)
    finally:
        for _ in range(3):
            st, r = L.call("config/devices/" + q(did), "PATCH", {"paused": False})
            if st == 200:
                resumed = round(time.time() - t0, 2)
                BOUNCE["resumed"] = True
                break
            time.sleep(1)
    if resumed is None:
        raise OpFail("the device stayed paused: PATCH paused false answered %s" % st)
    t1 = time.time()
    back = None
    after = ""
    while time.time() - t1 < 120:
        up, started = connection(L, did)
        if up:
            back = back or round(time.time() - t0, 2)
            if real_time(started):
                after = started
                break
            if time.time() - t1 > 15:
                break
        time.sleep(0.25)
    return {"dropped_after": dropped, "resumed_after": resumed, "back_after": back,
            "startedAt_before": before, "startedAt_after": after}


def op_status(a):
    L = Local()
    st, s = L.call("db/status?folder=" + q(a["fid"]))
    if st != 200 or not isinstance(s, dict):
        raise OpFail("db/status answered %s: %s" % (st, str(s)[:200]))
    out = {"status": {k: s.get(k) for k in STATUS_KEYS}, "views": {}, "at": time.time()}
    for did in a.get("peers", []):
        st, c = L.call("db/completion?folder=%s&device=%s" % (q(a["fid"]), q(did)))
        out["views"][did] = {k: c.get(k) for k in VIEW_KEYS} if st == 200 and isinstance(c, dict) else None
    return out


def op_scan(a):
    L = Local()
    st, r = L.call("db/scan?folder=" + q(a["fid"]), "POST", timeout=900)
    return {"code": st, "text": "" if st == 200 else str(r)[:300]}


def op_localchanged(a):
    """Every item db/localchanged lists, page by page."""
    L = Local()
    items, page, per = [], 1, 1000
    while True:
        r = L.must("db/localchanged?folder=%s&page=%d&perpage=%d" % (q(a["fid"]), page, per))
        got = r.get("files") or [] if isinstance(r, dict) else []
        for x in got:
            items.append({"name": x.get("name"), "type": x.get("type"), "deleted": bool(x.get("deleted")),
                          "size": x.get("size")})
        if len(got) < per:
            return {"items": items}
        page += 1


def op_revert(a):
    L = Local()
    st, r = L.call("db/revert?folder=" + q(a["fid"]), "POST", timeout=300)
    return {"code": st, "text": "" if st == 200 else str(r)[:300]}


def manifest_rows(root):
    """(path, kind) for every entry under root, kind "d", "l:TARGET" or
    "f:SHA256"; the marker directory .stfolder/ at the root left out, since its
    file carries each device's own creation time and never syncs (pilot,
    2026-10-10); sorted by the path's bytes, LC_ALL=C order."""
    rows, errors = [], []
    for dp, dns, fns in os.walk(root, onerror=lambda e: errors.append(str(e))):
        rel = os.path.relpath(dp, root)
        if rel == ".":
            dns[:] = [d for d in dns if d != ".stfolder"]
        for d in dns:
            p = os.path.join(dp, d)
            r = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(rel, d))
            rows.append((r, "l:" + os.readlink(p) if os.path.islink(p) else "d"))
        for n in fns:
            p = os.path.join(dp, n)
            r = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(rel, n))
            if os.path.islink(p):
                rows.append((r, "l:" + os.readlink(p)))
                continue
            h = hashlib.sha256()
            try:
                with open(p, "rb") as fh:
                    for chunk in iter(lambda: fh.read(1 << 20), b""):
                        h.update(chunk)
            except OSError as e:
                errors.append(str(e))
                continue
            rows.append((r, "f:" + h.hexdigest()))
    rows.sort(key=lambda x: x[0].encode("utf-8", "surrogateescape"))
    return rows, errors


def manifest_digest(rows):
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    for r, k in rows:
        h.update(("%s\t%s\n" % (r, k)).encode("utf-8", "surrogateescape"))
    return h.hexdigest()


def op_manifest(a):
    rows, errors = manifest_rows(a["path"])
    out = {"count": len(rows), "digest": manifest_digest(rows), "errors": errors[:5]}
    if a.get("full"):
        out["rows"] = rows
    return out


def op_fsck(a):
    """git fsck --connectivity-only, under GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, for every .git
    in the tree; nothing under a .git is walked."""
    root = a["path"]
    repos = []
    for dp, dns, fns in os.walk(root):
        if ".git" in dns or ".git" in fns:
            repos.append(dp)
        dns[:] = [d for d in dns if d != ".git" and not (dp == root and d == ".stfolder")]
    out = []
    for r in repos:
        rc, so, se = git_out(["-C", r, "fsck", "--connectivity-only", "--no-dangling", "--no-progress"],
                             timeout=1800)
        out.append({"repo": os.path.relpath(r, root), "rc": rc, "err": (se.strip() or so.strip())[:300]})
    return {"repos": out}


def op_trash(a):
    t = a["trash"]
    files = []
    for dp, dns, fns in os.walk(t):
        for n in fns:
            files.append(os.path.relpath(os.path.join(dp, n), t))
    return {"exists": os.path.isdir(t), "files": sorted(files)}


def op_delete(a):
    L = Local()
    st, r = L.call("config/folders/" + q(a["fid"]), "DELETE")
    return {"code": st, "text": "" if st == 200 else str(r)[:300], "absent": L.folder(a["fid"]) is None}


OPS = {"probe": op_probe, "post": op_post, "patch": op_patch, "share": op_share, "bounce": op_bounce,
       "status": op_status, "scan": op_scan, "localchanged": op_localchanged, "revert": op_revert,
       "manifest": op_manifest, "fsck": op_fsck, "trash": op_trash, "delete": op_delete}
WRITES = {"post", "patch", "share", "bounce", "revert", "delete", "scan"}


def remote_main(op, raw):
    """The remote mode: one operation, one JSON line, exit 0 always (ssh's 255
    must mean that ssh itself failed)."""
    try:
        if op not in OPS:
            raise OpFail("unknown operation %r" % op)
        out = OPS[op](json.loads(raw))
    except OpFail as e:
        out = {"error": str(e)}
    except Exception as e:      # a reading that could not finish is never health
        out = {"error": "%s: %s" % (type(e).__name__, e)}
    print(json.dumps(out))
    return 0


# =============================================================================
# The controller: runs on the writer
# =============================================================================
class Stop(Exception):
    """The run stops here. code 1: stopped (refused, a gate, a wait, his word);
    2: could not determine."""

    def __init__(self, msg, fix=None, code=1):
        Exception.__init__(self, msg)
        self.fix = fix
        self.code = code


class Unreachable(Exception):
    pass


def stamp():
    t = time.time()
    return time.strftime("%H:%M:%S", time.localtime(t)) + ".%03d" % int((t % 1) * 1000)


class Out:
    def __init__(self, log_path=None):
        self.log = None
        if log_path:
            try:
                self.log = open(log_path, "a", encoding="utf-8")
            except OSError as e:
                raise Stop("cannot append to the log %s: %s" % (log_path, e), code=2)

    def raw(self, text):
        print(text, flush=True)
        if self.log:
            self.log.write(text + "\n")
            self.log.flush()

    def say(self, tag, msg):
        label = {"OK": " OK ", "DO": " DO "}.get(tag, tag)
        self.raw("%s [%-4s] %s" % (stamp(), label, msg))

    def fix(self, msg):
        self.raw("%s        fix: %s" % (" " * 12, msg))

    def more(self, msg):
        self.raw("%s        %s" % (" " * 12, msg))


class Machine:
    """One machine of the cluster, reached in-process (this one) or over ssh."""

    def __init__(self, run, role, name, local=False):
        self.run = run
        self.role = role
        self.name = name
        self.local = local
        self.id = None
        self.door = None
        self.failed = set()

    def op(self, op, args, timeout=120, password=None):
        if self.local:
            if password is not None:
                globals()["_CONTROLLER_PASSWORD"] = password
            try:
                return OPS[op](args)
            except OpFail as e:
                raise Stop("%s: %s" % (self.name, e), code=2)
            finally:
                globals().pop("_CONTROLLER_PASSWORD", None)
        if not HOSTNAME_RE.fullmatch(self.name or ""):
            raise Unreachable("%r is a device name, not a host name ssh can be given" % self.name)
        doors = [self.name, self.name + "-vpn"]
        order = ([self.door] if self.door else []) + [d for d in doors if d != self.door and d not in self.failed]
        if op in WRITES and self.door:
            order = [self.door]      # a write never retries through another door
        errors = []
        for d in order:
            rc, out, err = self.run.ssh(d, op, args, timeout, password, connect=2 if d == self.name else 8)
            if rc == 255:
                self.failed.add(d)
                if self.door == d:
                    self.door = None
                errors.append("%s: %s" % (d, err))
                if op in WRITES:
                    break
                continue
            self.door = d
            try:
                data = json.loads(out.strip().splitlines()[-1])
            except (ValueError, IndexError):
                raise Stop("%s answered %s with something that is not this tool's JSON (exit %s%s)"
                           % (d, op, rc, (": " + err) if err else ""), code=2)
            if not isinstance(data, dict):
                raise Stop("%s answered %s with something that is not this tool's JSON" % (d, op), code=2)
            if data.get("error"):
                raise Stop("%s: %s" % (self.name, data["error"]), code=2)
            return data
        raise Unreachable("; ".join(errors) or "no door left to try")


def overlap(a, b):
    a, b = os.path.normpath(a), os.path.normpath(b)
    return a == b or a.startswith(b.rstrip(os.sep) + os.sep) or b.startswith(a.rstrip(os.sep) + os.sep)


def under(p, root):
    p, root = os.path.normpath(p), os.path.normpath(root)
    return p == root or p.startswith(root.rstrip(os.sep) + os.sep)


def in_git(name):
    return ".git" in name.split("/")


def unit_for(path):
    """The systemd mount unit for a plain path (systemd-escape --path)."""
    s = path.strip("/")
    s = "".join(c if c.isalnum() or c in "/_." else "\\x%02x" % ord(c) for c in s)
    return s.replace("/", "-") + ".mount"


def human(n):
    n = float(n or 0)
    for u in ("B", "KB", "MB", "GB"):
        if n < 1000 or u == "GB":
            return ("%d %s" % (n, u)) if u == "B" else ("%.1f %s" % (n, u))
        n /= 1000


class Run:
    def __init__(self, o):
        self.o = o
        self.out = Out(o["log"])
        self.nonce = secrets.token_hex(16)
        self.source = None
        self.fails = 0
        self.unknowns = 0
        self.created = []
        self.password = None
        self.W = Machine(self, "writer", None, local=True)
        self.H = self.R = None
        self.wprobe = self.hprobe = self.rprobe = None
        self.link = not o["hub_only"]
        self.held = {}         # role -> folder config at the start (redacted) or None
        self.shape = None
        self.trash = o["trash"]

    # --- plumbing -------------------------------------------------------------------
    def say(self, tag, msg):
        self.out.say(tag, msg)

    def ok(self, msg):
        self.say("OK", msg)

    def fail(self, msg, fix=None):
        self.fails += 1
        self.say("FAIL", msg)
        if fix:
            self.out.fix(fix)

    def check(self, cond, okmsg, failmsg, fix=None):
        if cond:
            self.ok(okmsg)
        else:
            self.fail(failmsg, fix)
        return bool(cond)

    def ssh(self, door, op, args, timeout, password, connect):
        if self.source is None:
            with open(os.path.realpath(sys.argv[0]), "r", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                self.source = fh.read()
        text = self.source if password is None else ("_CONTROLLER_PASSWORD = %r\n" % password) + self.source
        cmd = ["ssh", "-o", "BatchMode=yes", "-o", "ConnectTimeout=%d" % connect,
               "-o", "ServerAliveInterval=5", "-o", "ServerAliveCountMax=2", door,
               "python3", "-I", "-", "--remote", op, shlex.quote(json.dumps(args))]
        try:
            p = subprocess.run(cmd, input=text, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout + connect + 30)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            return 255, "", "no answer within %d s" % (timeout + connect + 30)
        except OSError as e:
            return 255, "", "cannot run ssh: %s" % e
        finally:
            text = None
        err = p.stderr.strip().splitlines()
        return p.returncode, p.stdout, err[-1] if err else ""

    def op(self, m, op, args, timeout=120, password=None):
        try:
            return m.op(op, args, timeout, password)
        except Unreachable as e:
            raise Stop("%s did not answer over ssh: %s" % (m.name, e), code=2,
                       fix="ssh -o BatchMode=yes %s true   # must answer; then run the same command again" % m.name)

    def name(self, did):
        for m in (self.W, self.H, self.R):
            if m is not None and m.id == did:
                return m.name
        return did[:7]

    def gate(self, question):
        self.say("GATE", question)
        if self.o["yes"]:
            self.say("GATE", "answered by --yes")
            return
        # two handles: text mode "r+" asks for a seekable file, which a
        # terminal is not, and would refuse every gate on a real one
        try:
            tin = open("/dev/tty", "r")
            tout = open("/dev/tty", "w")
        except OSError:
            raise Stop("no terminal to answer the gate on", fix="run it in your own shell, or pass --yes")
        try:
            tout.write("%s        Press Enter to proceed, Ctrl-C to stop: " % (" " * 12))
            tout.flush()
            line = tin.readline()
        finally:
            tin.close()
            tout.close()
        if not line:
            raise Stop("the terminal closed at the gate")
        self.say("GATE", "passed by Enter")

    def budget(self):
        pf = (self.wprobe or {}).get("path") or {}
        return (WAIT_FLOOR + (pf.get("bytes") or 0) / WAIT_RATE + (pf.get("files") or 0) * WAIT_PER_FILE) * WAIT_SCALE

    # --- preflight ---------------------------------------------------------------
    def args_ok(self):
        o = self.o
        self.say("NOTE", "== the arguments ==")
        self.check(ID_RE.fullmatch(o["id"]), "id %s: two groups of five over the cluster's alphabet" % o["id"],
                   "id %r is not two groups of five over a-z without i and l, and 2-9" % o["id"],
                   fix="python3 -c \"import secrets as s; a='abcdefghjkmnopqrstuvwxyz23456789'; "
                       "print('-'.join(''.join(s.choice(a) for _ in range(5)) for _ in range(2)))\"")
        lab = o["label"]
        self.check(lab and lab == lab.strip() and not any(ord(c) < 32 for c in lab),
                   "label %r" % lab, "label %r is empty, padded or holds a control character" % lab)
        for what, p in (("writer's path", o["wpath"]), ("reader's path", o["rpath"]), ("hub's path", o["hpath"])):
            self.check(os.path.isabs(p) and os.path.normpath(p) == p.rstrip("/") or p == "/",
                       "%s %s" % (what, p), "%s %r is not an absolute, normalised path" % (what, p))
        if o["trash"] is not None:
            self.check(os.path.isabs(o["trash"]), "trashcan %s" % o["trash"],
                       "trashcan %r is not an absolute path" % o["trash"])
        if self.fails:
            raise Stop("the arguments do not hold", code=2)
        for k in ("wpath", "rpath", "hpath", "trash"):
            if o[k] is not None:
                o[k] = os.path.normpath(o[k])
        self.trash = o["trash"]

    def identify(self):
        """This machine, the hub and the reader, by device names in the configs."""
        o = self.o
        self.say("NOTE", "== the machines ==")
        wp = self.op(self.W, "probe", {"fid": o["id"], "path": o["wpath"], "nonce": self.nonce,
                                       "walk": True, "git": True}, timeout=1800)
        self.wprobe = wp
        self.W.id = wp["myID"]
        names = {d["deviceID"]: d.get("name") or d["deviceID"][:7] for d in wp["devices"]}
        self.W.name = names.get(self.W.id) or wp["node"]
        if o["hub"]:
            ids = [i for i, n in names.items() if n == o["hub"] and i != self.W.id]
            if len(ids) != 1:
                raise Stop("no device here is named %r" % o["hub"], code=2)
            hub_id = ids[0]
        else:
            enc = set()
            for f in wp["folders"]:
                enc |= set(f["enc"])
            enc.discard(self.W.id)
            if len(enc) != 1:
                raise Stop("cannot tell the hub: %s carries the cluster password here"
                           % ("no device" if not enc else "more than one device (%s)" % ", ".join(sorted(names.get(i, i[:7]) for i in enc))),
                           fix="name it: --hub NAME (its device name in this machine's configuration)", code=2)
            hub_id = enc.pop()
        self.H = Machine(self, "hub", names.get(hub_id) or hub_id[:7])
        self.H.id = hub_id
        self.ok("this machine, the writer: %s (Syncthing %s, %s)" % (self.W.name, wp["version"], wp["config"]))
        hp = self.op(self.H, "probe", {"fid": o["id"], "path": o["hpath"], "mount": True})
        self.hprobe = hp
        if hp["myID"] != hub_id:
            raise Stop("ssh %s reached a Syncthing whose device is not the hub's (%s, not %s)"
                       % (self.H.door, hp["myID"][:7], hub_id[:7]), code=2)
        self.ok("the hub: %s over ssh %s (Syncthing %s, %s)" % (self.H.name, self.H.door, hp["version"], hp["config"]))
        hnames = {d["deviceID"]: d.get("name") or d["deviceID"][:7] for d in hp["devices"]}
        if self.W.id not in hnames:
            raise Stop("the hub does not know this machine as a device", code=2)
        if o["peer"]:
            ids = [i for i, n in list(names.items()) + list(hnames.items())
                   if n == o["peer"] and i not in (self.W.id, hub_id)]
            ids = sorted(set(ids))
            if len(ids) != 1:
                raise Stop("no device is named %r here or on the hub" % o["peer"], code=2)
            peer_id = ids[0]
        else:
            cands = [i for i in hnames if i not in (self.W.id, hub_id)]
            if len(cands) != 1:
                raise Stop("cannot tell the reader: the hub knows %d other devices" % len(cands),
                           fix="name it: --peer NAME", code=2)
            peer_id = cands[0]
        self.R = Machine(self, "reader", names.get(peer_id) or hnames.get(peer_id) or peer_id[:7])
        self.R.id = peer_id
        rp = self.op(self.R, "probe", {"fid": o["id"], "path": o["rpath"], "nonce": self.nonce,
                                       "walk": True, "git": True, "trash": o["trash"]}, timeout=1800)
        self.rprobe = rp
        if rp["myID"] != peer_id:
            raise Stop("ssh %s reached a Syncthing whose device is not the reader's" % self.R.door, code=2)
        self.ok("the reader: %s over ssh %s (Syncthing %s, %s)" % (self.R.name, self.R.door, rp["version"], rp["config"]))

    def check_machine(self, m, p, peers):
        """The settings every machine must have before a folder is shared."""
        opts = p["options"]
        self.check(not any(opts.get(k) for k in PHONE_HOME),
                   "%s: global announce, relays, NAT and crash reporting off" % m.name,
                   "%s: phone-home open: %s" % (m.name, ", ".join(k for k in PHONE_HOME if opts.get(k))),
                   fix="org/machines/syncthing.md -> \"Settings that must stay off\"")
        auto = [d.get("name") or d["deviceID"][:7] for d in p["devices"] if d.get("autoAcceptFolders")]
        self.check(not auto, "%s: autoAcceptFolders off for every device" % m.name,
                   "%s: autoAcceptFolders on for %s -- a folder could be accepted from its defaults, unversioned"
                   % (m.name, ", ".join(auto)),
                   fix="turn it off in %s's GUI: Remote Devices -> Edit -> Sharing -> Auto Accept" % m.name)
        devs = {d["deviceID"]: d for d in p["devices"]}
        for did in peers:
            n = self.name(did)
            if did not in devs:
                self.fail("%s: %s is not a device there" % (m.name, n),
                          fix="--hub-only, or add the device as rules.md -> ws-16 says" if did in (self.W.id, self.R.id) else None)
                continue
            self.check(not devs[did].get("paused"), "%s: device %s not paused" % (m.name, n),
                       "%s: device %s is paused (a bounce cut short leaves it so)" % (m.name, n),
                       fix="resume it in %s's GUI (Remote Devices -> %s -> Resume)" % (m.name, n))
            self.check(p["connected"].get(did), "%s: connected to %s" % (m.name, n),
                       "%s: not connected to %s" % (m.name, n),
                       fix="check Proton VPN's kill switch and the tailnet first (org/machines/syncthing.md)")

    def check_neighbours(self, m, p, path):
        """No other folder there with this label, or a path that contains or
        lies inside this one (both paths resolved on that machine)."""
        o = self.o
        real = (p.get("path") or {}).get("realpath") or path
        for f in p["folders"]:
            if f["id"] == o["id"]:
                continue
            if f["label"] == o["label"]:
                self.fail("%s: folder %s already carries the label %r" % (m.name, f["id"], o["label"]))
            if overlap(f["path"], real):
                self.fail("%s: folder %r at %s contains or lies inside %s" % (m.name, f["label"], f["path"], path))

    def spec_problems(self, f, role):
        o = self.o
        probs = []
        types = {"writer": ("sendreceive",), "hub": ("receiveencrypted",),
                 "reader": ("sendreceive", "receiveonly")}[role]
        if f.get("type") not in types:
            probs.append("type %s" % f.get("type"))
        want_path = {"writer": o["wpath"], "hub": o["hpath"], "reader": o["rpath"]}[role]
        if os.path.normpath(f.get("path") or "") != os.path.normpath(want_path):
            probs.append("path %s" % f.get("path"))
        if f.get("label") != o["label"]:
            probs.append("label %r" % f.get("label"))
        if f.get("maxConflicts") != MAX_CONFLICTS:
            probs.append("maxConflicts %s" % f.get("maxConflicts"))
        if not f.get("fsWatcherEnabled") or f.get("fsWatcherDelayS") != WATCH_DELAY_S:
            probs.append("watcher %s/%s s" % (f.get("fsWatcherEnabled"), f.get("fsWatcherDelayS")))
        if f.get("rescanIntervalS") != RESCAN_S:
            probs.append("rescan %s s" % f.get("rescanIntervalS"))
        if f.get("paused"):
            probs.append("paused")
        v = f.get("versioning") or {}
        if role == "hub":
            if v.get("type") != "staggered" or (v.get("params") or {}).get("maxAge") != "31536000":
                probs.append("versioning %s %s" % (v.get("type"), v.get("params")))
            if (f.get("minDiskFree") or {}) != HUB_MIN_DISK_FREE:
                probs.append("minDiskFree %s" % f.get("minDiskFree"))
        elif role == "writer" or v.get("type") != "trashcan":
            if v.get("type"):
                probs.append("versioning %s" % v.get("type"))
        else:
            if f.get("type") == "receiveonly" or v.get("type") == "trashcan":
                if (v.get("params") or {}).get("cleanoutDays") != "0" or not os.path.isabs(v.get("fsPath") or "") \
                        or (self.trash and os.path.normpath(v.get("fsPath")) != os.path.normpath(self.trash)):
                    probs.append("trashcan %s at %s" % (v.get("params"), v.get("fsPath")))
        if f.get("type") == "receiveonly" and v.get("type") != "trashcan":
            probs.append("receiveonly without its trashcan")
        have = {d["deviceID"]: d.get("encryptionPassword") == "<set>" for d in f.get("devices", [])}
        me = {"writer": self.W, "hub": self.H, "reader": self.R}[role].id
        if role == "hub":
            required = {me: False, self.W.id: False, self.R.id: False}
            optional = {}
        else:
            other = self.R.id if role == "writer" else self.W.id
            required = {me: False, self.H.id: True}
            optional = {other: False} if self.link else {}
        for did, enc in required.items():
            if did not in have:
                probs.append("does not share with %s" % self.name(did))
            elif have[did] != enc:
                probs.append("%s's entry %s a password" % (self.name(did), "lacks" if enc else "carries"))
        for did, enc in have.items():
            if did in required:
                continue
            if did in optional and enc == optional[did]:
                continue
            probs.append("shares with %s" % self.name(did))
        return probs

    def describe(self, f):
        v = f.get("versioning") or {}
        ver = "none" if not v.get("type") else "%s %s%s" % (
            v["type"], ",".join("%s=%s" % kv for kv in sorted((v.get("params") or {}).items())),
            (" at " + v["fsPath"]) if v.get("fsPath") else "")
        devs = " + ".join("%s%s" % (self.name(d["deviceID"]), " (password set)" if d.get("encryptionPassword") == "<set>" else "")
                          for d in f.get("devices", []))
        extra = ", minDiskFree %s %s" % ((f.get("minDiskFree") or {}).get("value"), (f.get("minDiskFree") or {}).get("unit")) \
            if f.get("type") == "receiveencrypted" else ""
        return "%s at %s, label %r, maxConflicts %s, watcher %s s, rescan %s s, versioning %s%s, devices %s" % (
            f.get("type"), f.get("path"), f.get("label"), f.get("maxConflicts"), f.get("fsWatcherDelayS"),
            f.get("rescanIntervalS"), ver, extra, devs)

    def preflight(self):
        o = self.o
        self.args_ok()
        self.identify()
        W, H, R = self.W, self.H, self.R
        wp, hp, rp = self.wprobe, self.hprobe, self.rprobe
        self.say("NOTE", "== preflight: the three machines ==")
        self.check_machine(W, wp, [H.id] + ([R.id] if self.link else []))
        self.check_machine(H, hp, [W.id, R.id])
        self.check_machine(R, rp, [H.id] + ([W.id] if self.link else []))
        self.check_roles()

        self.say("NOTE", "== preflight: the folder %s %r ==" % (o["id"], o["label"]))
        for m, p in ((W, wp), (H, hp), (R, rp)):
            self.held[m.role] = p["folder"]
            self.check_neighbours(m, p, {"writer": o["wpath"], "hub": o["hpath"], "reader": o["rpath"]}[m.role])
        held = tuple(r for r in ("writer", "hub", "reader") if self.held[r] is not None)
        if held not in ((), ("writer",), ("writer", "hub"), ("writer", "hub", "reader")):
            self.fail("held by %s alone: a run leaves bigfed, bigfed and the hub, or all three"
                      % " and ".join(self.name({"writer": W, "hub": H, "reader": R}[r].id) for r in held),
                      fix="undo it (the line below), then run again with a new hub directory")
        for m in (W, H, R):
            f = self.held[m.role]
            if f is None:
                self.ok("%s: does not hold the folder yet" % m.name)
                continue
            probs = self.spec_problems(f, m.role)
            self.check(not probs, "%s: holds it as specified, to verify rather than re-create: %s" % (m.name, self.describe(f)),
                       "%s: holds it differently: %s" % (m.name, "; ".join(probs)),
                       fix="inspect it in %s's GUI; undo it (the line below) if it is not wanted" % m.name)

        # the writer's path
        wf = wp["path"]
        if self.check(wf["isdir"], "%s: %s is a directory: %d files, %s" % (W.name, o["wpath"], wf.get("files") or 0, human(wf.get("bytes"))),
                      "%s: %s is not a directory" % (W.name, o["wpath"])):
            self.markers(W, wf)
        # the hub's path
        hf = hp["path"]
        if self.held["hub"] is None:
            self.check(not hf["exists"], "%s: %s does not exist yet (hub-3)" % (H.name, o["hpath"]),
                       "%s: %s exists; a new hub folder gets a new, empty directory (hub-3)" % (H.name, o["hpath"]),
                       fix="choose a new HUB-PATH; the old directory stays until he deletes it")
            if not hf["exists"]:
                self.check(hf.get("ancestor_isdir"), "%s: %s, its nearest existing ancestor, is a directory" % (H.name, hf.get("ancestor")),
                           "%s: %s lies under %s, which is not a directory" % (H.name, o["hpath"], hf.get("ancestor")),
                           fix="choose a HUB-PATH under a directory")
        mf = hp.get("mount") or {}
        if mf.get("applies"):
            if not mf.get("exists"):
                self.fail("%s: %s does not exist, so the sync volume is not mounted" % (H.name, mf["sync"]),
                          fix="ssh %s 'sudo systemctl start %s'" % (H.name, unit_for(mf["sync"])))
            else:
                self.check(mf.get("target") == mf["sync"],
                           "%s: %s is on the dedicated volume (%s, %s)" % (H.name, o["hpath"], mf.get("fstype"), mf.get("source")),
                           "%s: %s lies on %s (%s), not on a volume mounted at %s -- the sync volume is not mounted"
                           % (H.name, o["hpath"], mf.get("target"), mf.get("fstype"), mf["sync"]),
                           fix="ssh %s 'sudo systemctl start %s'" % (H.name, unit_for(mf["sync"])))
        else:
            self.ok("%s: %s is not under %s, no volume to check" % (H.name, o["hpath"], mf.get("sync")))
        # the reader's path, and the shape
        self.decide_shape()
        # the passwords
        self.check_passwords()
        # a repository at a folder's root
        for m, p, path in ((W, wp, o["wpath"]), (R, rp, o["rpath"])):
            g = p.get("git") or {}
            if "marker_ignore_rc" in g:
                self.check(g["marker_ignore_rc"] == 0, "%s: the repository at %s ignores .stfolder/" % (m.name, path),
                           "%s: the repository at %s does not ignore .stfolder/ (check-ignore exit %s), so `git add -A` would commit the marker"
                           % (m.name, path, g["marker_ignore_rc"]),
                           fix="add the line .stfolder/ to the global exclude, org/claude-config/git/ignore (rules.md -> mig-4, 2026-10-10)")
        if self.fails:
            raise Stop("the preflight refused (%d)" % self.fails)
        if self.unknowns:
            raise Stop("the preflight could not determine %d reading(s)" % self.unknowns, code=2)

    def check_roles(self):
        """This machine reads `gsync.role = writer`; the reader shows a role
        other than writer, or a readerRepo naming READER-PATH (the pilot's
        shape). An absent role on the reader refuses: it is the host file that
        has not travelled yet (pilot.md, the fold-in's step 4 before its step
        6), and gsync reads an absent role as a writer."""
        W, R, o = self.W, self.R, self.o
        g = self.wprobe.get("git") or {}
        if g.get("role_rc", 0) > 1:
            self.unknown("%s: git could not read gsync.role (exit %s: %s)" % (W.name, g["role_rc"], g.get("role_err")),
                         fix="git config --show-origin --get gsync.role")
        else:
            self.check(g.get("role") == "writer", "%s: gsync.role reads writer" % W.name,
                       "%s: gsync.role reads %r, so this is not the writer; the tool runs on bigfed"
                       % (W.name, g.get("role") or "(absent)"),
                       fix="git config --show-origin --get gsync.role   # configs/git/hosts/<machine>.inc through ~/.config/git/host.inc")
        g = self.rprobe.get("git") or {}
        fix = ("set it in configs/git/hosts/%s.inc -- role = reader, or readerRepo = <name> for one repository -- "
               "and pull it on %s; there `git config --show-origin --get gsync.role` reads it (rules.md -> fedxps-2)"
               % (R.name, R.name))
        if g.get("role_rc", 0) > 1 or g.get("reader_repo_rc", 0) > 1:
            self.unknown("%s: git could not read its gsync keys (exit %s: %s)" % (
                R.name, max(g.get("role_rc", 0), g.get("reader_repo_rc", 0)),
                g.get("role_err") or g.get("reader_repo_err")), fix="ssh %s git config --show-origin --get-regexp '^gsync[.]'" % R.name)
        elif g.get("role"):
            self.check(g["role"] != "writer", "%s: gsync.role reads %s" % (R.name, g["role"]),
                       "%s: gsync.role reads writer: two writers" % R.name, fix=fix)
        elif g.get("reader_repo_match"):
            self.ok("%s: no gsync.role, and readerRepo names %s" % (R.name, o["rpath"]))
        else:
            self.fail("%s: no gsync.role%s, so nothing there marks it a reader of %s yet" % (
                R.name, (" and readerRepo names %s alone" % ", ".join(g.get("reader_repos")))
                if g.get("reader_repos") else "", o["rpath"]), fix=fix)

    def unknown(self, msg, fix=None):
        self.unknowns += 1
        self.say("WARN", msg)
        if fix:
            self.out.fix(fix)

    def markers(self, m, f):
        if f.get("walk_errors"):
            self.fail("%s: parts of %s could not be read: %s" % (m.name, f["path"], "; ".join(f["walk_errors"])))
        self.check(not f.get("markers_below_count"), "%s: no .stfolder marker under %s" % (m.name, f["path"]),
                   "%s: %d .stfolder marker(s) under %s: %s -- a folder inside the folder (mig-3 gate 4)"
                   % (m.name, f.get("markers_below_count") or 0, f["path"], ", ".join(f.get("markers_below") or [])),
                   fix="remove that folder from Syncthing's configuration on every machine first")
        self.check(not f.get("marker_above"), "%s: no .stfolder marker above %s" % (m.name, f["path"]),
                   "%s: %s lies inside the folder at %s" % (m.name, f["path"], f.get("marker_above")))
        if f.get("marker_here") and self.held[m.role] is None:
            self.fail("%s: %s holds a .stfolder marker, but no folder here claims it" % (m.name, f["path"]),
                      fix="never make a marker by hand (org/machines/syncthing.md); find the folder it belonged to")

    def decide_shape(self):
        o, R = self.o, self.R
        rf = self.rprobe["path"]
        held = self.held["reader"]
        if held is not None:
            v = held.get("versioning") or {}
            if held.get("type") == "receiveonly" or v.get("type") == "trashcan":
                self.shape = "join"
                if self.trash is None:
                    self.trash = v.get("fsPath")
                self.say("NOTE", "shape: join, resumed (%s holds it %s%s)" % (R.name, held.get("type"),
                         " with its trashcan" if v.get("type") == "trashcan" else ""))
            else:
                self.shape = "fresh"
                self.say("NOTE", "shape: the reader holds it send-receive already; the common tail remains")
            if rf.get("isdir"):
                self.markers(R, rf)
            return
        if not rf["exists"] or (rf["isdir"] and rf.get("empty")):
            self.shape = "fresh"
            self.ok("shape: fresh -- %s's %s is %s" % (R.name, o["rpath"], "absent" if not rf["exists"] else "empty"))
            if o["trash"] is not None:
                self.fail("--trash names a trashcan, but %s's path is %s: the fresh shape" % (R.name, "absent" if not rf["exists"] else "empty"),
                          fix="check READER-PATH; leave --trash out for a fresh folder")
            if rf.get("marker_above"):
                self.fail("%s: %s lies inside the folder at %s" % (R.name, o["rpath"], rf["marker_above"]))
            if not rf["exists"] and not rf.get("ancestor_isdir"):
                self.fail("%s: %s lies under %s, which is not a directory" % (R.name, o["rpath"], rf.get("ancestor")),
                          fix="check READER-PATH")
            return
        if not rf["isdir"]:
            self.fail("%s: %s exists and is not a directory" % (R.name, o["rpath"]))
            return
        self.shape = "join"
        self.ok("shape: join -- %s's %s holds %d entries, %d files, %s" % (R.name, o["rpath"], rf.get("entries") or 0,
                rf.get("files") or 0, human(rf.get("bytes"))))
        self.markers(R, rf)
        wf = self.wprobe["path"]
        if wf.get("isdir"):
            self.check(not wf.get("empty"), "%s: %s holds the writer's copy" % (self.W.name, o["wpath"]),
                       "%s: %s is empty while the reader's holds files: a join would revert the reader's whole tree"
                       % (self.W.name, o["wpath"]))
        if self.trash is None:
            self.fail("the join shape needs a trashcan for the reader's revert",
                      fix="--trash DIR: absolute, on %s, outside the folder and outside every Syncthing folder" % R.name)
            return
        tf = self.rprobe.get("trash") or {}
        self.check(os.path.isabs(self.trash) and not under(tf.get("realpath") or self.trash, rf.get("realpath") or o["rpath"]),
                   "%s: trashcan %s lies outside the folder" % (R.name, self.trash),
                   "%s: trashcan %s lies inside the folder %s" % (R.name, self.trash, o["rpath"]))
        self.check(not tf.get("marker_above"), "%s: trashcan %s lies outside every Syncthing folder" % (R.name, self.trash),
                   "%s: trashcan %s lies inside the folder at %s" % (R.name, self.trash, tf.get("marker_above")))
        self.check(not tf.get("exists") or (tf.get("isdir") and tf.get("empty")),
                   "%s: trashcan %s is %s" % (R.name, self.trash, "absent" if not tf.get("exists") else "empty"),
                   "%s: trashcan %s exists and is not an empty directory" % (R.name, self.trash),
                   fix="name a new directory for --trash")

    def check_passwords(self):
        W, R = self.W, self.R
        nw, nr = self.wprobe["passwords"], self.rprobe["passwords"]
        if nw > 1:
            self.fail("%s holds %d different cluster passwords; the contract says one" % (W.name, nw),
                      fix="org/machines/syncthing.md -> \"The password\"")
        elif nw == 1:
            self.ok("%s: the cluster password is read from its configuration, never printed" % W.name)
        else:
            self.say("NOTE", "%s holds no encrypted folder: the password is asked for once, at the first write" % W.name)
            if self.o["yes"] or self.o["dry_run"]:
                if not self.o["dry_run"]:
                    self.fail("the first encrypted folder of the cluster needs the password typed on a terminal",
                              fix="run it yourself, without --yes")
        if nr > 1:
            self.fail("%s holds %d different cluster passwords; the contract says one" % (R.name, nr),
                      fix="org/machines/syncthing.md -> \"The password\"")
        elif nr == 1 and nw == 1:
            self.check(hmac.compare_digest(self.wprobe.get("pw_digest") or "", self.rprobe.get("pw_digest") or "x"),
                       "%s: holds the same cluster password (compared under a nonce, never printed)" % R.name,
                       "%s: its cluster password differs from %s's; a mismatch drops the whole device connection" % (R.name, W.name),
                       fix="org/machines/syncthing.md -> \"The password\"")
        elif nr == 0 and self.held["reader"] is None:
            self.say("NOTE", "%s holds no encrypted folder: %s's password reaches it inside the program text over ssh"
                     % (R.name, W.name))

    # --- the plan ------------------------------------------------------------------
    def bodies(self):
        o = self.o
        W, H, R = self.W, self.H, self.R
        base = {"label": o["label"], "fsWatcherEnabled": True, "fsWatcherDelayS": WATCH_DELAY_S,
                "rescanIntervalS": RESCAN_S, "maxConflicts": MAX_CONFLICTS, "paused": False, "id": o["id"]}
        link_now = self.link and self.shape == "fresh"
        bw = dict(base, path=o["wpath"], type="sendreceive", versioning=dict(NO_VERSIONING),
                  devices=[{"deviceID": W.id}, {"deviceID": H.id}] + ([{"deviceID": R.id}] if link_now else []))
        bh = dict(base, path=o["hpath"], type="receiveencrypted", versioning=dict(HUB_VERSIONING),
                  minDiskFree=dict(HUB_MIN_DISK_FREE),
                  devices=[{"deviceID": H.id}, {"deviceID": W.id}, {"deviceID": R.id}])
        if self.shape == "join":
            br = dict(base, path=o["rpath"], type="receiveonly",
                      versioning={"type": "trashcan", "params": {"cleanoutDays": "0"}, "cleanupIntervalS": 3600,
                                  "fsPath": self.trash, "fsType": "basic"},
                      devices=[{"deviceID": R.id}, {"deviceID": H.id}])
        else:
            br = dict(base, path=o["rpath"], type="sendreceive", versioning=dict(NO_VERSIONING),
                      devices=[{"deviceID": R.id}, {"deviceID": H.id}] + ([{"deviceID": W.id}] if link_now else []))
        return bw, bh, br

    def plan(self):
        W, H, R = self.W, self.H, self.R
        bw, bh, br = self.bodies()
        P = lambda s: self.say("PLAN", s)
        verb = lambda role: "verify" if self.held[role] is not None else "POST /rest/config/folders"
        devs = lambda b, enc: " + ".join(self.name(d["deviceID"]) + (" (password)" if d["deviceID"] == enc else "") for d in b["devices"])
        P("shape %s; waits up to %d s each" % (self.shape, self.budget()))
        P("%s: %s: sendreceive, devices %s; then its scan idle" % (W.name, verb("writer"), devs(bw, H.id)))
        P("%s: %s: receiveencrypted, staggered maxAge 31536000, minDiskFree 1 %%, devices %s" % (H.name, verb("hub"), devs(bh, None)))
        P("%s: PATCH /rest/config/devices/<%s> paused true, %g s, false (the bounce); then the hub idle with %s's set"
          % (W.name, H.name, HOLD, W.name))
        if self.shape == "join":
            P("gate: %s joins receive-only; no Claude session there until the switch (mig-3 gate 6)" % R.name)
            P("%s: %s: receiveonly, trashcan cleanoutDays 0 at %s, devices %s" % (R.name, verb("reader"), self.trash, devs(br, H.id)))
            P("%s: the bounce of %s; gate 7: its view of the hub at the hub's sequence, global counts and bytes as %s's" % (R.name, H.name, W.name))
            P("%s: GET /rest/db/localchanged, every path printed; a path outside a .git stops the run%s"
              % (R.name, " (--allow-outside: goes on)" if self.o["allow_outside"] else ""))
            P("gate; %s: POST /rest/db/revert; then no receive-only change left" % R.name)
            P("gate 9: manifests of both trees equal, git fsck clean in every .git on %s, the trashcan holding what was listed" % R.name)
            P("gate; %s: PATCH type sendreceive; %s's and %s's sequences unchanged after %g s" % (R.name, H.name, W.name, WATCH))
            P("%s: PATCH versioning none (the trashcan directory stays)" % R.name)
            if self.link:
                P("%s and %s: PATCH devices + each other (the direct link, ws-16)" % (W.name, R.name))
        else:
            P("%s: %s: sendreceive, devices %s" % (R.name, verb("reader"), devs(br, H.id)))
            P("%s: the bounce of %s" % (R.name, H.name))
        P("all three idle, nothing needed, every view 100 at the device's own sequence")

    # --- writes ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    def post(self, m, body, enc_to, password_mode=None):
        self.say("DO", "%s: POST /rest/config/folders (%s)" % (m.name, body["type"]))
        pw = None
        if password_mode == "controller":
            pw = self.password
        r = self.op(m, "post", {"body": body, "enc_to": enc_to, "password": password_mode or "own"}, password=pw)
        pw = None
        if r["code"] != 200:
            raise Stop("%s: the POST answered %s: %s" % (m.name, r["code"], r["text"]))
        self.created.append(m.role)
        self.held[m.role] = r["folder"]
        f = r["folder"]
        if f is None:
            raise Stop("%s: the folder is not there after a POST that answered 200" % m.name, code=2)
        probs = self.spec_problems(f, m.role)
        if probs:
            raise Stop("%s: read back differently from the POST: %s" % (m.name, "; ".join(probs)))
        self.ok("%s: read back as specified: %s" % (m.name, self.describe(f)))

    def bounce(self, m):
        self.say("DO", "%s: bounce of %s: PATCH paused true, hold %g s, PATCH paused false" % (m.name, self.H.name, HOLD))
        r = self.op(m, "bounce", {"device": self.H.id, "hold": HOLD}, timeout=int(HOLD) + 180)
        if r.get("dropped_after") is None or r.get("back_after") is None:
            raise Stop("%s: the bounce was not seen: dropped after %s s, back after %s s"
                       % (m.name, r.get("dropped_after"), r.get("back_after")), code=2)
        self.ok("%s: the connection to %s dropped %.1f s after the pause, resumed at %.1f s, back at %.1f s (startedAt %s)"
                % (m.name, self.H.name, r["dropped_after"], r["resumed_after"], r["back_after"],
                   r.get("startedAt_after") or "not yet read"))

    # --- readings and waits ------------------------------------------------------------
    def read(self, m, peers):
        return self.op(m, "status", {"fid": self.o["id"], "peers": peers})

    def line(self, m, r):
        s = r["status"]
        parts = ["%s %s need=%s files=%s dirs=%s links=%s bytes=%s seq=%s" % (
            m.name, s.get("state"), s.get("needTotalItems"), s.get("globalFiles"), s.get("globalDirectories"),
            s.get("globalSymlinks"), s.get("globalBytes"), s.get("sequence"))]
        if s.get("pullErrors"):
            parts.append("pullErrors=%s" % s["pullErrors"])
        if s.get("error"):
            parts.append("error=%r" % s["error"])
        if s.get("receiveOnlyTotalItems"):
            parts.append("receive-only changes=%s" % s["receiveOnlyTotalItems"])
        for did, v in (r.get("views") or {}).items():
            if v is None:
                parts.append("view of %s unread" % self.name(did))
            else:
                parts.append("view of %s %s%% need=%s seq=%s %s" % (self.name(did), v.get("completion"), v.get("needItems"),
                                                                   v.get("sequence"), v.get("remoteState")))
        return " | ".join(parts)

    def wait(self, what, machines, cond, budget=None):
        """Read `machines` ({role: (Machine, peers)}) every POLL seconds until
        cond(readings) returns (True, ...) on two rounds in a row with the same
        sequences; a reading line whenever it changes."""
        budget = budget if budget is not None else self.budget()
        t0 = time.time()
        shown = {}
        last_print = 0.0
        prev = None
        misses = 0
        while True:
            rd = {}
            try:
                for role, (m, peers) in machines.items():
                    rd[role] = self.read(m, peers)
                misses = 0
            except Stop as e:
                # a wait can run half an hour: one failed reading (an ssh
                # hiccup) is read again, both doors, three times in a row at most
                misses += 1
                if e.code != 2 or misses > 3 or time.time() - t0 > budget:
                    raise
                self.say("WARN", "a reading failed (%s); reading again" % e)
                for m, _ in machines.values():
                    m.failed.clear()
                time.sleep(max(POLL, 5.0))
                continue
            ok, why = cond(rd)
            now = time.time()
            for role, (m, peers) in machines.items():
                ln = self.line(m, rd[role])
                if shown.get(role) != ln or now - last_print > 30:
                    self.say("WAIT" if not ok else "READ", ln)
                    shown[role] = ln
                    last_print = now
            key = tuple((rd[r]["status"].get("sequence"), rd[r]["status"].get("globalFiles"),
                         rd[r]["status"].get("needTotalItems")) for r in sorted(rd))
            if ok and key == prev:
                self.ok("%s, %.1f s" % (what, now - t0))
                return rd
            prev = key if ok else None
            if now - t0 > budget:
                raise Stop("%s did not hold within %d s: %s" % (what, budget, why),
                           fix="run the same command again to keep waiting; it verifies what is made")
            time.sleep(POLL)

    @staticmethod
    def idle(s):
        return s.get("state") == "idle" and not s.get("needTotalItems") and not s.get("pullErrors") and not s.get("errors")

    def view_ok(self, rd, a, b, ids):
        v = (rd[a].get("views") or {}).get(ids[b])
        sb = rd[b]["status"]
        return v is not None and v.get("completion") == 100 and not v.get("needItems") and not v.get("needDeletes") \
            and v.get("remoteState") == "valid" and v.get("sequence") == sb.get("sequence")

    def counts_match(self, ws, hs):
        return hs.get("globalFiles") == ws.get("globalFiles") and \
            (hs.get("globalDirectories") or 0) + (hs.get("globalSymlinks") or 0) == \
            (ws.get("globalDirectories") or 0) + (ws.get("globalSymlinks") or 0)

    def ids(self):
        return {"writer": self.W.id, "hub": self.H.id, "reader": self.R.id}

    def wait_writer_scan(self):
        def cond(rd):
            s = rd["writer"]["status"]
            return s.get("state") == "idle" and not s.get("errors"), "state %s" % s.get("state")
        self.wait("%s scanned its copy" % self.W.name, {"writer": (self.W, [])}, cond)

    def wait_hub(self):
        ids = self.ids()

        def cond(rd):
            ws, hs = rd["writer"]["status"], rd["hub"]["status"]
            if not (self.idle(ws) and self.idle(hs)):
                return False, "not idle with nothing needed"
            if not self.counts_match(ws, hs):
                return False, "the hub's counts are not %s's" % self.W.name
            if not (self.view_ok(rd, "writer", "hub", ids) and self.view_ok(rd, "hub", "writer", ids)):
                return False, "a view is not at 100 at the device's own sequence"
            return True, ""
        self.wait("the hub holds %s's set" % self.W.name,
                  {"writer": (self.W, [self.H.id]), "hub": (self.H, [self.W.id])}, cond)

    def hub_settled_once(self):
        ids = self.ids()
        rd = {"writer": self.read(self.W, [self.H.id]), "hub": self.read(self.H, [self.W.id])}
        ws, hs = rd["writer"]["status"], rd["hub"]["status"]
        return self.idle(hs) and self.counts_match(ws, hs) and self.view_ok(rd, "hub", "writer", ids) \
            and self.view_ok(rd, "writer", "hub", ids)

    def reader_has_hub_index(self):
        ids = self.ids()
        rd = {"reader": self.read(self.R, [self.H.id]), "hub": self.read(self.H, [])}
        v = (rd["reader"].get("views") or {}).get(ids["hub"]) or {}
        return v.get("remoteState") == "valid" and v.get("sequence") == rd["hub"]["status"].get("sequence") \
            and (rd["hub"]["status"].get("sequence") or 0) > 0

    def wait_gate7(self):
        """The reader's view of the hub carries the hub's own sequence (its
        index has arrived), and its global counts and bytes are bigfed's."""
        ids = self.ids()

        def cond(rd):
            ws, hs, rs = rd["writer"]["status"], rd["hub"]["status"], rd["reader"]["status"]
            v = (rd["reader"].get("views") or {}).get(ids["hub"]) or {}
            if not (self.idle(ws) and self.idle(hs) and self.idle(rs)):
                return False, "not idle with nothing needed"
            if not (v.get("remoteState") == "valid" and v.get("sequence") == hs.get("sequence") and (hs.get("sequence") or 0) > 0):
                return False, "the hub's index has not reached %s (its view of the hub at sequence %s, the hub at %s)" % (
                    self.R.name, v.get("sequence"), hs.get("sequence"))
            for k in ("globalFiles", "globalDirectories", "globalSymlinks", "globalBytes"):
                if rs.get(k) != ws.get(k):
                    return False, "%s's %s %s, %s's %s" % (self.R.name, k, rs.get(k), self.W.name, ws.get(k))
            if not self.counts_match(ws, hs):
                return False, "the hub's counts are not %s's" % self.W.name
            return True, ""
        return self.wait("gate 7: the hub's index on %s, its global counts and bytes %s's" % (self.R.name, self.W.name),
                         {"writer": (self.W, []), "hub": (self.H, []), "reader": (self.R, [self.H.id])}, cond)

    def wait_final(self):
        ids = self.ids()
        pairs = [("writer", "hub"), ("hub", "writer"), ("reader", "hub"), ("hub", "reader")]
        if self.link:
            pairs += [("writer", "reader"), ("reader", "writer")]
        peers = {r: [ids[b] for a, b in pairs if a == r] for r in ("writer", "hub", "reader")}

        def cond(rd):
            ws, hs, rs = rd["writer"]["status"], rd["hub"]["status"], rd["reader"]["status"]
            if not all(self.idle(x) for x in (ws, hs, rs)):
                return False, "not idle with nothing needed everywhere"
            for k in ("globalFiles", "globalDirectories", "globalSymlinks", "globalBytes"):
                if rs.get(k) != ws.get(k):
                    return False, "%s's %s %s, %s's %s" % (self.R.name, k, rs.get(k), self.W.name, ws.get(k))
            if not self.counts_match(ws, hs):
                return False, "the hub's counts are not %s's" % self.W.name
            bad = ["%s->%s" % (self.name(ids[a]), self.name(ids[b])) for a, b in pairs if not self.view_ok(rd, a, b, ids)]
            if bad:
                return False, "views not at 100 at the device's own sequence: %s" % ", ".join(bad)
            return True, ""
        return self.wait("all three converged, every view at 100",
                         {"writer": (self.W, peers["writer"]), "hub": (self.H, peers["hub"]),
                          "reader": (self.R, peers["reader"])}, cond)

    # --- the join's middle -------------------------------------------------------------
    def inspect_and_revert(self):
        o, R = self.o, self.R
        items = self.op(R, "localchanged", {"fid": o["id"]}, timeout=600)["items"]
        st = self.read(R, [])["status"]
        self.say("READ", "%s: GET /rest/db/localchanged: %d items (receiveOnlyTotalItems %s)"
                 % (R.name, len(items), st.get("receiveOnlyTotalItems")))
        outside = []
        for it in items:
            tag = "deleted " if it["deleted"] else ""
            kind = (it.get("type") or "").replace("FILE_INFO_TYPE_", "").lower()
            self.out.more("%s%s %s" % (tag, kind, it["name"]))
            if not in_git(it["name"]):
                outside.append(it["name"])
        if len(items) != (st.get("receiveOnlyTotalItems") or 0):
            raise Stop("%s lists %d local changes but counts %s" % (R.name, len(items), st.get("receiveOnlyTotalItems")), code=2)
        if outside:
            if not o["allow_outside"]:
                self.fail("%d of them lie outside a .git: %s" % (len(outside), ", ".join(outside[:10])
                                                                 + (" ..." if len(outside) > 10 else "")))
                raise Stop("the revert would move %s's own files outside .git into the trashcan; a look first" % R.name,
                           fix="look at them on %s; to revert them all into %s, run the same command with --allow-outside"
                               % (R.name, self.trash))
            self.say("NOTE", "%d outside a .git, reverted by --allow-outside" % len(outside))
        else:
            self.ok("every local change lies inside a .git")
        if not items:
            self.ok("%s: nothing to revert" % R.name)
            return []
        self.gate("the revert next: %s's %d local changes go into the trashcan %s" % (R.name, len(items), self.trash))
        self.say("DO", "%s: POST /rest/db/revert" % R.name)
        r = self.op(R, "revert", {"fid": o["id"]})
        if r["code"] != 200:
            raise Stop("%s: the revert answered %s: %s" % (R.name, r["code"], r["text"]))

        def cond(rd):
            s = rd["reader"]["status"]
            done = self.idle(s) and not s.get("receiveOnlyTotalItems") and not s.get("receiveOnlyChangedFiles")
            return done, "receive-only changes %s" % s.get("receiveOnlyTotalItems")
        self.wait("%s reverted: idle, nothing needed, no receive-only change" % R.name, {"reader": (R, [])}, cond)
        return items

    def gate9(self, items):
        o, W, R = self.o, self.W, self.R
        st = self.read(R, [])["status"]
        self.check(not any(st.get(k) for k in ("receiveOnlyChangedFiles", "receiveOnlyChangedDirectories",
                                                "receiveOnlyChangedSymlinks", "receiveOnlyChangedDeletes",
                                                "receiveOnlyTotalItems")),
                   "gate 9: %s has no receive-only change" % R.name,
                   "gate 9: %s still counts receive-only changes: %s" % (R.name, {k: st.get(k) for k in st if k.startswith("receiveOnly")}))
        mw = self.op(W, "manifest", {"path": o["wpath"], "full": True}, timeout=3600)
        mr = self.op(R, "manifest", {"path": o["rpath"]}, timeout=3600)
        for m, mf in ((W, mw), (R, mr)):
            if mf["errors"]:
                self.fail("%s: parts of the tree could not be read: %s" % (m.name, "; ".join(mf["errors"])))
        if mw["digest"] == mr["digest"] and mw["count"] == mr["count"]:
            self.ok("gate 9: the manifests are equal: %d entries, sha256 %s, .stfolder/ left out" % (mw["count"], mw["digest"][:16]))
        else:
            full = self.op(R, "manifest", {"path": o["rpath"], "full": True}, timeout=3600)
            a, b = dict(map(tuple, mw["rows"])), dict(map(tuple, full["rows"]))
            diff = [k for k in sorted(set(a) | set(b), key=lambda x: x.encode("utf-8", "surrogateescape")) if a.get(k) != b.get(k)]
            self.fail("gate 9: the manifests differ in %d entries (%d here, %d there)" % (len(diff), mw["count"], mr["count"]))
            for k in diff[:20]:
                self.out.more("%s: %s | %s" % (k, (a.get(k) or "-")[:18], (b.get(k) or "-")[:18]))
        fk = self.op(R, "fsck", {"path": o["rpath"]}, timeout=7200)["repos"]
        bad = [x for x in fk if x["rc"] != 0]
        self.check(not bad, "gate 9: git fsck --connectivity-only clean on %s in %d repositor%s (%s)"
                   % (R.name, len(fk), "y" if len(fk) == 1 else "ies", ", ".join(x["repo"] for x in fk) or "none"),
                   "gate 9: git fsck fails on %s in %s" % (R.name, "; ".join("%s (exit %s: %s)" % (x["repo"], x["rc"], x["err"]) for x in bad)))
        want = sorted(it["name"] for it in items if not it["deleted"] and (it.get("type") or "").endswith("FILE"))
        tr = self.op(R, "trash", {"trash": self.trash})
        missing = [n for n in want if n not in set(tr["files"])]
        self.check(not missing, "gate 9: the trashcan %s holds the %d file(s) listed (%d files there)" % (self.trash, len(want), len(tr["files"])),
                   "gate 9: the trashcan %s lacks %d listed file(s): %s" % (self.trash, len(missing), ", ".join(missing[:10])))
        if self.fails:
            raise Stop("gate 9 does not hold; %s is still receive-only, nothing has been sent" % R.name)

    def switch(self):
        o, W, H, R = self.o, self.W, self.H, self.R
        self.gate("the switch next: %s's folder to sendreceive" % R.name)
        before = {m.role: self.read(m, [])["status"].get("sequence") for m in (H, W, R)}
        self.say("READ", "sequences before the switch: %s %s, %s %s, %s %s"
                 % (H.name, before["hub"], W.name, before["writer"], R.name, before["reader"]))
        self.say("DO", "%s: PATCH /rest/config/folders/%s type sendreceive" % (R.name, o["id"]))
        r = self.op(R, "patch", {"fid": o["id"], "fields": {"type": "sendreceive"}})
        if r["code"] != 200 or (r["folder"] or {}).get("type") != "sendreceive":
            raise Stop("%s: the switch answered %s, type now %s" % (R.name, r["code"], (r["folder"] or {}).get("type")))
        self.held["reader"] = r["folder"]
        self.ok("%s: read back type sendreceive" % R.name)
        self.say("WAIT", "watching the sequences for %g s" % WATCH)
        time.sleep(WATCH)
        after = {m.role: self.read(m, [])["status"].get("sequence") for m in (H, W, R)}
        self.say("READ", "sequences after %g s: %s %s, %s %s, %s %s"
                 % (WATCH, H.name, after["hub"], W.name, after["writer"], R.name, after["reader"]))
        if after["hub"] != before["hub"] or after["writer"] != before["writer"]:
            raise Stop("something was sent at the switch: %s %s -> %s, %s %s -> %s; %s keeps its trashcan versioning for a look"
                       % (H.name, before["hub"], after["hub"], W.name, before["writer"], after["writer"], R.name),
                       fix="read %s's db/remoteneed and the hub's versions before anything else" % W.name)
        self.ok("nothing sent at the switch: %s's sequence %s and %s's %s unchanged" % (H.name, after["hub"], W.name, after["writer"]))

    def versioning_off(self):
        R = self.R
        self.say("DO", "%s: PATCH /rest/config/folders/%s versioning none" % (R.name, self.o["id"]))
        r = self.op(R, "patch", {"fid": self.o["id"], "fields": {"versioning": dict(NO_VERSIONING)}})
        f = r["folder"] or {}
        if r["code"] != 200 or (f.get("versioning") or {}).get("type"):
            raise Stop("%s: versioning answered %s, type now %r" % (R.name, r["code"], (f.get("versioning") or {}).get("type")))
        self.held["reader"] = f
        self.ok("%s: versioning none; the trashcan %s stays until he has looked through it" % (R.name, self.trash))

    def share_link(self):
        for m, other in ((self.W, self.R), (self.R, self.W)):
            f = self.held[m.role] or {}
            if any(d["deviceID"] == other.id for d in f.get("devices", [])):
                continue
            self.say("DO", "%s: PATCH /rest/config/folders/%s devices + %s (the direct link)" % (m.name, self.o["id"], other.name))
            r = self.op(m, "share", {"fid": self.o["id"], "device": other.id})
            if r["code"] != 200 or not r["hub_entry_unchanged"]:
                raise Stop("%s: the share answered %s, the hub's entry %s" % (
                    m.name, r["code"], "unchanged" if r["hub_entry_unchanged"] else "CHANGED"))
            self.held[m.role] = r["folder"]
            probs = self.spec_problems(r["folder"], m.role)
            if probs:
                raise Stop("%s: read back differently: %s" % (m.name, "; ".join(probs)))
            self.ok("%s: shares with %s, the hub's entry unchanged: %s" % (m.name, other.name, self.describe(r["folder"])))

    # --- the run ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    def create(self):
        o = self.o
        W, H, R = self.W, self.H, self.R
        if self.held["writer"] is None and self.wprobe["passwords"] == 0:
            self.password = ask_password(o, self.out)
            if self.rprobe["passwords"] == 1:
                d = hmac.new(self.nonce.encode(), self.password.encode("utf-8", "surrogateescape"), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()
                if not hmac.compare_digest(d, self.rprobe.get("pw_digest") or ""):
                    raise Stop("that is not the password %s already holds; nothing has been created" % R.name)
        bw, bh, br = self.bodies()
        self.say("NOTE", "== %s, the writer ==" % W.name)
        if self.held["writer"] is None:
            self.post(W, bw, H.id, "controller" if self.password else None)
        else:
            self.say("SKIP", "%s: holds it as specified" % W.name)
        self.wait_writer_scan()
        self.say("NOTE", "== %s, the hub ==" % H.name)
        if self.held["hub"] is None:
            self.post(H, bh, None)
        else:
            self.say("SKIP", "%s: holds it as specified" % H.name)
        if set(self.created) & {"writer", "hub"} or not self.hub_settled_once():
            self.bounce(W)
        else:
            self.say("SKIP", "%s: the hub already holds %s's set; no bounce" % (W.name, W.name))
        self.wait_hub()
        self.say("NOTE", "== %s, the reader (%s) ==" % (R.name, self.shape))
        if self.held["reader"] is None:
            if self.shape == "join":
                self.gate("%s joins receive-only next; no Claude session there from here to the switch (mig-3 gate 6)" % R.name)
            pwmode = None
            if self.rprobe["passwords"] == 0:
                pwmode = "controller"
                if self.password is None:
                    self.password = read_own_password()
            self.post(R, br, H.id, pwmode)
        else:
            self.say("SKIP", "%s: holds it as specified" % R.name)
        if "reader" in self.created or not self.reader_has_hub_index():
            self.bounce(R)
        else:
            self.say("SKIP", "%s: already holds the hub's index; no bounce" % R.name)
        f = self.held["reader"]
        if self.shape == "join" and f.get("type") == "receiveonly":
            self.wait_gate7()
            items = self.inspect_and_revert()
            self.gate9(items)
            self.switch()
        if self.shape == "join" and ((self.held["reader"].get("versioning") or {}).get("type") == "trashcan"):
            self.versioning_off()
        if self.link:
            self.share_link()
        self.say("NOTE", "== the three ==")
        self.wait_final()
        self.ok("done: %s %r on %s, %s and %s" % (o["id"], o["label"], W.name, H.name, R.name))
        self.say("NOTE", "add its row to org/machines/syncthing.md today: a folder's id is half its key")
        if self.shape == "join":
            self.say("NOTE", "the trashcan %s on %s stays until he has looked through it" % (self.trash, R.name))


def read_own_password():
    """This machine's one cluster password, for a reader that holds none: read
    from config.xml into memory only."""
    pws = Local().passwords()
    if len(pws) != 1:
        raise Stop("this machine holds %d cluster passwords, not one" % len(pws))
    return pws[0]


def ask_password(o, out):
    """Once in the life of the cluster: from /dev/tty, echo off, twice."""
    try:
        open("/dev/tty").close()
    except OSError:
        raise Stop("the first encrypted folder needs the password typed on a terminal", fix="run it in your own shell")
    out.say("NOTE", "no encrypted folder exists here yet, so this is the ONE time the password is asked for:")
    out.more("copy it out of Proton Pass now; it is never echoed, and never stored but in the two")
    out.more("workstations' own config.xml")
    pw = getpass.getpass("  password: ")
    if not pw:
        raise Stop("empty password; nothing has been created")
    if any(c.isspace() for c in pw):
        raise Stop("that holds whitespace, so it is not a generated password -- almost certainly this command "
                   "line, still on the clipboard. Nothing has been created.")
    for a in (o["id"], o["wpath"], o["rpath"], o["hpath"]):
        if a and a in pw:
            raise Stop("that holds this command's own arguments, so it is the command line rather than the "
                       "password. Nothing has been created.")
    if getpass.getpass("  confirm : ") != pw:
        raise Stop("the two entries differ; nothing has been created")
    out.say("OK", "accepted (%d characters): this is now the cluster password" % len(pw))
    return pw


def undo_line(o):
    return "syncthing-addfolder --undo %s %s" % (shlex.quote(o["id"]), shlex.quote(o["label"]))


def print_undo(run):
    o = run.o
    held = [r for r in ("hub", "writer", "reader") if run.held.get(r) is not None]
    if not held and len(run.held) == 3:
        run.out.more("undo: nothing to undo, no machine holds the folder")
        return
    if len(run.held) < 3:
        run.out.more("undo, if any machine holds it (the hub first, then this machine, then the reader): %s" % undo_line(o))
        return
    run.out.more("undo, the hub first, then %s, then the reader: %s" % (run.W.name, undo_line(o)))
    stays = []
    if run.held.get("hub") is not None:
        stays.append("the hub's blobs at %s, its marker renamed .stfolder.removed-<time> (a later folder takes a new directory, hub-3)" % o["hpath"])
    if run.held.get("writer") is not None:
        stays.append("%s's tree at %s" % (run.W.name, o["wpath"]))
    if run.held.get("reader") is not None:
        stays.append("%s's tree at %s" % (run.R.name if run.R else "the reader", o["rpath"]))
    if run.trash and run.shape == "join":
        stays.append("the trashcan %s" % run.trash)
    run.out.more("  what stays on disk: " + "; ".join(stays))


def create_main(o):
    run = Run(o)
    run.say("NOTE", "syncthing-addfolder %s %r, %s, on %s%s" % (
        o["id"], o["label"], time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z"), os.uname().nodename,
        ", dry run" if o["dry_run"] else ""))
    try:
        run.preflight()
        run.plan()
        if o["dry_run"]:
            run.say("OK", "dry run: the preflight passed and nothing was written")
            return 0
        run.gate("the parameters above, the plan above: the first write is next")
        run.create()
        return 0
    except Stop as e:
        run.say("STOP", str(e))
        if e.fix:
            run.out.fix(e.fix)
        if o["dry_run"]:
            run.out.more("dry run: nothing was written")
        else:
            run.out.more("resume: the same command again; it verifies what is made and goes on")
            print_undo(run)
        return e.code
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        run.say("STOP", "interrupted")
        if BOUNCE.get("pause_sent"):
            if BOUNCE.get("resumed"):
                run.out.more("the bounce under way here was cut short; its resume answered 200")
            else:
                run.out.more("the bounce under way here was cut short and its resume did not answer: "
                             "the hub device may stay paused here, which the next run's preflight reads")
                run.out.fix("resume it in this machine's GUI (Remote Devices -> %s -> Resume)" % (run.H.name if run.H else "the hub"))
        print_undo(run)
        return 1
    except Exception as e:      # a run that could not finish is never a success
        run.say("STOP", "could not finish: %s: %s" % (type(e).__name__, e))
        print_undo(run)
        return 2


def undo_main(o):
    """--undo ID LABEL: remove the folder from the hub, then this machine,
    then the reader; refuses a folder whose label is not LABEL."""
    run = Run(o)
    run.say("NOTE", "syncthing-addfolder --undo %s %r, %s, on %s%s" % (
        o["id"], o["label"], time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z"), os.uname().nodename,
        ", dry run" if o["dry_run"] else ""))
    try:
        if not ID_RE.fullmatch(o["id"]) and not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,64}", o["id"]):
            raise Stop("id %r does not look like a folder id" % o["id"], code=2)
        W = run.W
        wp = run.op(W, "probe", {"fid": o["id"]})
        W.id = wp["myID"]
        names = {d["deviceID"]: d.get("name") or d["deviceID"][:7] for d in wp["devices"]}
        W.name = names.get(W.id) or wp["node"]
        f = wp["folder"]
        hub_ids = [i for i, n in names.items() if o["hub"] and n == o["hub"]]
        if not hub_ids:
            enc = set()
            for g in wp["folders"]:
                enc |= set(g["enc"])
            enc.discard(W.id)
            if f is not None:
                enc = {d["deviceID"] for d in f["devices"] if d.get("encryptionPassword") == "<set>"} or enc
            hub_ids = sorted(enc)
        if len(hub_ids) != 1:
            raise Stop("cannot tell the hub", fix="name it: --hub NAME", code=2)
        run.H = Machine(run, "hub", names.get(hub_ids[0]))
        run.H.id = hub_ids[0]
        hp = run.op(run.H, "probe", {"fid": o["id"]})
        hnames = {d["deviceID"]: d.get("name") or d["deviceID"][:7] for d in hp["devices"]}
        peers = [i for i in hnames if i not in (W.id, run.H.id)]
        if o["peer"]:
            peers = [i for i in set(hnames) | set(names) if (names.get(i) or hnames.get(i)) == o["peer"]]
        if len(peers) != 1:
            raise Stop("cannot tell the reader", fix="name it: --peer NAME", code=2)
        run.R = Machine(run, "reader", names.get(peers[0]) or hnames.get(peers[0]))
        run.R.id = peers[0]
        probes = {"hub": hp, "writer": wp}
        try:
            probes["reader"] = run.op(run.R, "probe", {"fid": o["id"]})
        except Stop as e:
            probes["reader"] = None
            run.say("WARN", "%s: %s" % (run.R.name, e))
        todo = []
        for role, m in (("hub", run.H), ("writer", W), ("reader", run.R)):
            p = probes[role]
            if p is None:
                continue
            f = p["folder"]
            run.held[role] = f
            if f is None:
                run.ok("%s: does not hold %s" % (m.name, o["id"]))
                continue
            if f.get("label") != o["label"]:
                raise Stop("%s holds %s with the label %r, not %r: nothing removed" % (m.name, o["id"], f.get("label"), o["label"]))
            v = f.get("versioning") or {}
            if v.get("type") == "trashcan":
                run.trash, run.shape = v.get("fsPath"), "join"
            run.say("PLAN", "%s: DELETE /rest/config/folders/%s (%s at %s)" % (m.name, o["id"], f.get("type"), f.get("path")))
            todo.append((role, m, f))
        if not todo:
            run.ok("nothing to undo")
            return 0 if probes["reader"] is not None else 2
        if o["dry_run"]:
            run.ok("dry run: nothing removed")
            return 0
        run.gate("remove the folder from the configurations above, in that order; every file stays on disk")
        for role, m, f in todo:
            run.say("DO", "%s: DELETE /rest/config/folders/%s" % (m.name, o["id"]))
            r = run.op(m, "delete", {"fid": o["id"]})
            if r["code"] != 200 or not r["absent"]:
                raise Stop("%s: the DELETE answered %s: %s" % (m.name, r["code"], r["text"]))
            run.ok("%s: removed from the configuration; %s stays on disk%s" % (
                m.name, f.get("path"), ", its marker renamed .stfolder.removed-<time>" if role == "hub" else ""))
        if run.trash:
            run.say("NOTE", "%s's trashcan %s stays" % (run.R.name, run.trash))
        if probes["reader"] is None:
            raise Stop("%s did not answer; run the same --undo again when it does" % run.R.name, code=2)
        run.ok("undone")
        return 0
    except Stop as e:
        run.say("STOP", str(e))
        if e.fix:
            run.out.fix(e.fix)
        return e.code
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        run.say("STOP", "interrupted")
        return 1


def usage(code):
    print(__doc__.split("\n\nThe successor")[0])
    sys.exit(code)


def parse(argv):
    o = {"trash": None, "allow_outside": False, "hub_only": False, "hub": None, "peer": None,
         "yes": False, "dry_run": False, "log": None, "undo": False}
    pos = []
    takes = {"--trash": "trash", "--hub": "hub", "--peer": "peer", "--log": "log"}
    flags = {"--allow-outside": "allow_outside", "--hub-only": "hub_only", "--yes": "yes",
             "--dry-run": "dry_run", "--undo": "undo"}
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a in ("-h", "--help"):
            usage(0)
        elif a == "--":
            pos += argv[i + 1:]
            break
        elif a in takes:
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                raise Stop("%s needs a value" % a, code=2)
            o[takes[a]] = argv[i + 1]
            i += 1
        elif a.split("=", 1)[0] in takes and "=" in a:
            o[takes[a.split("=", 1)[0]]] = a.split("=", 1)[1]
        elif a in flags:
            o[flags[a]] = True
        elif a.startswith("-") and a != "-":
            raise Stop("unknown option %s (try -h)" % a, code=2)
        else:
            pos.append(a)
        i += 1
    want = 2 if o["undo"] else 5
    if len(pos) != want:
        raise Stop("%s takes %d arguments, not %d (try -h)" % ("--undo" if o["undo"] else "syncthing-addfolder", want, len(pos)), code=2)
    o["id"], o["label"] = pos[0], pos[1]
    if not o["undo"]:
        o["wpath"], o["rpath"], o["hpath"] = pos[2], pos[3], pos[4]
    return o


def _interrupt(signum, frame):
    raise KeyboardInterrupt()


def main(argv):
    if argv[:1] == ["--remote"]:
        if len(argv) != 3:
            print(json.dumps({"error": "--remote takes OP and one JSON argument"}))
            return 0
        return remote_main(argv[1], argv[2])
    try:
        o = parse(argv)
    except Stop as e:
        print("syncthing-addfolder: %s" % e, file=sys.stderr)
        return e.code
    # SIGINT too: a parent that ignores it (a background job) must not make
    # Ctrl-C a no-op here, since the bounce's resume rides on it
    for s in (signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP):
        signal.signal(s, _interrupt)
    try:
        return undo_main(o) if o["undo"] else create_main(o)
    except Stop as e:           # the log could not be opened
        print("syncthing-addfolder: %s" % e, file=sys.stderr)
        return e.code


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
